<table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" align="center" bgcolor="#000000">
  <tr>
    <td>
      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#414f6e" style="border-collapse: collapse" bordercolor="#414f6e">
        <tr>
          <td align="center" class="text"><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Happy 4th of July</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><p align="center"><br><img border="0" src="../images/ccdhap4th.jpg"></p><br><p align="left">A quick visit to the Plane of Fire last night for some armor upgrades.&nbsp; As usual, we came, we saw, we won, we left.&nbsp; Pyronis, Quavonis &amp; Magmaton fell in quick succession - providing the following new toys:</p><br><ul><li>Elemental Chain Boots Pattern - Feelmore</li><br>  <li>Elemental Leather Boots Pattern - Hechicera</li><br>  <li>Elemental Plate Vambraces Mold - Rasttan </li><br>  <li>Elemental Chain Sleeves Pattern - Gluas</li><br>  <li>Elemental Plate Gauntlets Mold - Grimblades &amp; Sorchaa</li><br></ul><br>Here's a tip for today: <b>DON'T PLAY EVERQUEST</b>  Go spend time with family, friends & do RL stuff.&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Friday, July 04, 2003 at 05:29 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">VM goes Old School</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><P>Tuesday night was retro-night at Club VM. This was also billed as "A night in Luclin with friends." Now, I'll be brutally honest, I basically skipped the entire Luclin expansin playing Dark Age of Camelot, which meant that Tuesday night I got my <A href="http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?id=7898" target=_blank>Emperor Ssraeshza</A> cherry popped. I'm sure that the Emperor fight was probably a whole lot more exciting before the launch of Planes of Power and the advent of 5 new levels and ungodly amounts of AA points. I'm sure that a 3 Cleric, 1 Druid CH team wouldn't have cut it pre-PoP either. And I'm pretty sure that a flawless kill given that sort of healing power would have been virtually impossible. I'm equally sure that the loot probably wouldn't have been as crappy as it was last night.</P>
<CENTER>
<TABLE id=AutoNumber1 style="BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse" borderColor=#111111 cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 border=0>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD width="100%"><IMG height=181 src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/lootpics/White_Ornate_Chain_Bridle.gif" width=400 border=0></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD width="100%">
<P align=center>Grats Genalen</P>
<P align=center>&nbsp;</P></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD width="100%"><IMG height=184 src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/lootpics/Shield_of_Mental_Fortitude.gif" width=405 border=0> </TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD width="100%">
<P align=center>Grats Eppie &amp; Darmond</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>Of course, all good raids are accompanied by some equally...interesting comments.&nbsp; To wit:</P>
<DIV align=center>
<CENTER>
<TABLE id=AutoNumber2 style="BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse" borderColor=#111111 cellSpacing=3 cellPadding=3 width="60%" border=0>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD width="100%">
<P align=center><IMG height=20 src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/screenshots/Kalakar_Baby.gif" width=552 border=0></P></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD width="100%">
<P align=center><IMG height=33 src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/screenshots/Xelera_Baby.gif" width=552 border=0></P></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD width="100%">
<P align=center>Calling Dr. Freud, calling Dr. Freud - it appears that our Necromancers have some unresolved issues with their Mommy's.</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER></DIV>
<P><STRONG>Today's News &amp; Notes:</STRONG></P>
<UL>
<LI><B>COIRNAV ESCAPES FROM EVERQUEST: </B>According to <A href="http://www.cnn.com/2003/WORLD/americas/07/02/chile.science.reut/index.html" target=_blank>this article</A> on the CNN website, Chilean scientists are baffled by the appearance of "<SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px">...a huge, gelatinous sea creature found washed up on the southern Pacific coast and were seeking international help identifying the mystery specimen".&nbsp; Believe it....or not?</SPAN> 
<LI><B>IT'S PROTECTED SPEECH...SO THERE: </B>A former Intel worker who "spammed" his former colleagues with e-mails criticizing his former employer had his day in the California Supreme Court ... and won.&nbsp; According to the ruling, the "...<SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px">barrage of e-mails sent by a fired Intel worker disparaging his former employer did not constitute trespassing"</SPAN>.&nbsp; <A href="http://www.cnn.com/2003/LAW/07/01/email.speech.ap/index.html" target=_blank>The article</A> is on the CNN website.</LI></UL>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Wednesday, July 02, 2003 at 03:58 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Where have all the mobs gone?</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><P>Well...it's official folks. Planes of Power has passed the point of critical mass. Four raid forces are in the Elemental Planes, and maybe four more are at the point where they are spending more time working on flags than gearing up. Which means that decent raid mobs have become a rare spawn once again. A thought occurred to me while we were waiting to send <A href="http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?id=11023" target=_blank>Krziik the Mighty</A> to a watery grave. </P>
<P>How cool would it be to introduce instancing (a la Lost Dungeons of Norrath) into the existing game? Feel like taking on Agnarr tonight? No problem - grab all your flagged members, head on over to the EQ Dungeon Master and away you go. Notice I said "flagged members". Here's the beauty of this system. For exp groups - you don't need the flags for any zones up to Plane of Tactics (current setup), but if you want to take down Agnarr, then by God, you'll do it with only the people who are flagged. Eliminate the whole non-flagged ratio system for raids. Since you can do the flag mob anytime you want, backflagging becomes less of a chore, and adds to the variety of the game. </P>
<P>Extend instancing to everything post-Kunark, and now the only thing standing in the way of a guild's advancement is the amount of time they are willing to expend to learn the encounters until they defeat them.&nbsp; I doubt Sony would ever go for something like this on the scale I have proposed - but think of how much bad blood this could eliminate...<BR></P>
<P>As I said before, Krziik the Mighty died a painful death last night. On the way there, Shilude picked up a nice new toy:</P>
<CENTER>
<TABLE id=AutoNumber1 style="BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse" borderColor=#111111 cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 border=0>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD width="100%"><IMG height=183 src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/lootpics/Kelp_Hilted_Mace.gif" width=397 border=0>&nbsp;</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER>
<P><BR><STRONG>New Guild Members:</STRONG></P>
<UL>
<LI>Tovarich (Warrior) 
<LI>Vaghris (Rogue) 
<LI>Legelis (Rogue) 
<LI>Dojamun (Druid)</LI></UL>
<P><STRONG>Sad Farewell:</STRONG></P>
<P>It is with a heavy heart that we bid farewell to Starlee &amp; Sindian.&nbsp; Real Life has cruelly intervened to deprive us of two stellar guildmates.&nbsp; Be well both of you - you will be sorely missed.&nbsp; You will always be&nbsp;in our hearts and prayers.</P>
<P><STRONG>Today's News &amp; Notes:<BR></P></STRONG>
<UL>
<LI>Jurors Friday evening sentenced Chante Mallard to 50 years for the murder of a homeless man she hit with her car and then left to die embedded in the windshield. Mallard was sentenced to 10 years for tampering with evidence. The sentences will serve concurrently. 
<LI>The federal government Friday launched a national "do-not-call" registry aimed at stopping most telemarketing phone calls to people who regard the sales pitches as invasive and want them blocked.</LI></UL>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Saturday, June 28, 2003 at 05:45 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Promotions ... </span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Another very quiet night in VM-ville.  We spent the night in Torment farming pieces for another Saryn key.  The highlights of the evening were the officer promotions as well as guildinvites for two new members.<br>So without further ado...<br><br><b>New Members</b><br><ul><li>Millikin (Ranger)</li><li>Washou (Druid)</li></ul>Welcome to the guild, both of you.<br><br><b>Officer Promotions</b><br><ul><li>Galeni</li><li>Xelera</li><li>Genalen (Lead Tank)</li><li>Keawen (Recruit Officer)</li><li>Shaekee (Guild Scribe)</li><li>Eadric (Raid Leader)</li></ul>Congratulations to all the new officers.<br><br><b>Harry Potter Update</b><br>Tovarich is about 1/4 of the way through the book.  No, he doesn't know who dies yet.<br><br><b>In other news...</b><br><ul><li>Sally Ride, America's first woman in space, was inducted into the U.S. Astronaut Hall of Fame on Saturday, almost 20 years to the day that she rocketed into history</li><li>Chief Justice William H. Rehnquist, 78, and Justice Sandra Day O'Connor, 73, are the main objects of retirement speculation because of their ages and their presumed desire to allow a Republican president to pick a successor.</li><li>A federal district court dismissed a request by the one-time plaintiff known as "Jane Roe" to reconsider the landmark U.S. Supreme Court decision that legalized abortion 30 years ago</li><li>A city firefighter in Pontiac, MI has been accused of pointing a gun at his wife when she tried to stop him from watching Internet pornography.</li>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Shaekee</a> on Sunday, June 22, 2003 at 06:37 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Slow day at the office...</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Slow night in the land of VM.  Very few worthwhile mobs were up, so we basically wandered over to Bastion of KarnorsThunderCastle to pick up bits and pieces for Agnarr key(s).  Brynju Thunderclap was about as much of a challenge as being able to tell left from right.  Oh wait, for <b>Eadric</b> that would be a challenge following this classic:<br><br><blockquote><font color="cyan">Eadric: Everyone hang a left and go upstairs - stop at the monks</font><br><i>Raid obediently trots along, runs into three mobs, starts fighting</i><font color="cyan"><br>Vis Maior Monks (in unison): Left?  Dude - we're going right...<br>Eadric: Oops - my bad.  I meant right everyone.</blockquote></font><br>Yeah - thanks a lot there Eadric Zoolander.  Tomorrow he will show off <b>MAGNUM</b> and think that he's really really amazingly disgustingly goodlooking...which he isn't.<br><br>Loot was pretty rare - Thunderclap dropped a couple of these - <br><a targer="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=24645">Wicked Shank</a> to the delight of Lokkin and Feelmore (grats both of you).<br><br>And I leave you with this confession from Eppie - not sure why he decided to share with the world but...ok Pink Pally.  <p align="center"><img src="http://www.vismaiorguild.org/screenshots/Eppie_Herpes.gif" border="0"></p><br>'Nuff said.</font>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Shaekee</a> on Friday, June 20, 2003 at 18:37 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">New Management, Same Old Story ...</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">As a warm up for the weekend's festivities, the Vis Maior Express made brief stops in Drunder, Doomfire and Reef of Coirnav last night.  Guest stars for last night's whistle stop tour included:<br><ul><li>Tallon Zek</li><li>Vallon Zek</li><li>Babnoxis, the Spider Queen</li><li>Magmaton</li><li>Hydrotha</li></ul><br>Another perfect 5 for 5 night, including a flawless Magmaton kill - all in all, not a bad start for Elyda's first night as Guild Leader.<br><br>The Loot:<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=27989">Warmaster's Recurved Longbow</a> - Grats Millikin<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=9462">Mask fo the Insightful</a> - Grats Viciado & Wilas<br>Elemental Silk Bracelet Pattern - Grats Leelale<br><a target="_blank" href="http://lucy.fnord.net/item.html?id=7767">Necklace of Reflected Flame</a> - Grats Genalen<br>Elemental Silk Sleeve Pattern - Grats Starlee & Wakit<br><br>Topics o' the Day - The Hulk, Harry Potter & Sex and the City.<br><ul><li>The Hulk: OK, based on the inside scoop - don't expect another Spider-Man.  Apparently the movie isn't what you might expect.  Fans looking for the action-packed feature a la Spider-Man might well be disappointed.</li><li>Harry Potter - the fifth book is out this weekend.  I have to admit, several weeks ago I gave serious thought to camping out at the local Barnes & Noble to pick up a copy at midnight (which Tovarich would have probably finished by 4 a.m. at the rate he reads!)  Then common sense took over as I headed over to Amazon.com to pre-order a copy.  Book Report coming soon...</li><li>Sex and the City -  The sixth (and apparently final) season kicks off on Sunday.Say it ain't so!!!  More fun, follies and frolics with the four femmes fatales from the streets of NYC.</li></ul>So the Outlook for this weekend?  Mad fun!<br><br><B>BREAKING NEWS</B><br>Remember the Hot Topic from two days ago?  Orrin Hatch's brilliant proposal to destroy end-user PC's for using illegal software?  Well, looks like Orrin may have to terminate his web servers first.  According to <a target="_blank" href="http://www.wired.com/news/politics/0,1283,59305,00.html">this story</a> on Wired.com's website, Herr Hatch is guilty of a little software piracy on his official US Senator website.  Game, set and match the good guys.  Remember John 8:7 Orrin?  <blockquote>He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone.</blockquote>  Or perhaps Luke 6:42 <blockquote>Either how canst thou say to thy brother, Brother, let me pull out the mote that is in thine eye, when thou thyself beholdest not the beam that is in thine own eye? Thou hypocrite, cast out first the beam out of thine own eye, and then shalt thou see clearly to pull out the mote that is in thy brother's eye.</blockquote><br>Translation:  <b>OOPS!!!!</b>  You blew it Orrin.  Thanks for playing, drive through.&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Shaekee</a> on Friday, June 20, 2003 at 03:36 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Congratulations Elyda</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Please join me in congratulating Elyda as she assumes the role of Guild Leader of Vis Maior.&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Shaekee</a> on Thursday, June 19, 2003 at 11:36 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Vex Thal ... and other news</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Nostalgic visit to Luclin_timesink_01 aka Vex Thal for the usual dose of fun, frolics and loot. Pretty much a ho-hum raid, so I won't bore everyone with the gory details.<BR><BR>Instead, I want to talk about an article from the Los Angeles Business Journal written by Laura Dunphy back in March of 2000. The title of the article was "Loyalty? What's That?"  The original article is <A href="http://www.findarticles.com/cf_dls/m5072/13_22/61645158/p1/article.jhtml" target=_blank>here</A> if you're interested in reading it. I have modified the article's wording ever so slightly to apply to the world of Norrath, so with apologies to Ms Dunphy ...<BR><BR><br><BLOCKQUOTE><FONT color=cyan>The first day in a new guild has always brought lots of expectations to fulfil and new people to meet.<BR><BR>These days, it can even bring dreams of moving on to an even more uber guild.<BR><BR>OK, the turnaround might not be that sudden, but the growing number of guilds with access to the Plane of Time has resulted in frequent guild-hopping, with loot and supposedly the "lure of a new challenge" as the driving force.<BR><BR>Tagging with a new guild with Plane of Time access can increase the possibility of "Phat Lewtz" immeasurably meaning loyalty isn't what it used to be.<BR><BR>"Traditional terms of loyalty have changed. What you find are guildmates who are much more loyal to their own advancement and their marketability than to a guild," said an anonymous ex-officer of Vis Maior who secretly transferred servers in order to join a guild with Plane of Time access behind everyone's back.  "There are very, very strong toons who have had three to five changes in three years. The rewards, both in terms of loot and perceived prestige are quite compelling today."<BR><BR>"Many people change guilds because their current guild have hit a bump in the road, and cannot immediately overcome the major flag obstacles that could easily be surpassed by leaving for another guild, such as Afterlife, Enlightened Dark or Township Rebellion", said an anonymous member of Vis Maior. "The sense of betrayal caused by these people leaving has an damaging effect on morale. Although my contention is that by guild-hopping in order to advance, these people have shown that they don't have the guts or the desire to work for their rewards. They want things handed to them by someone else. From my perspective, we're better off without them."<BR><BR>"I've seen guilds take 2 months to achieve a major kill and be very proud of their achievement," said a former guild leader of Vis Maior. "Meanwhile, the guild-hoppers like myself are already two kills ahead by moving around to whichever guild(s) have the hot hand. You tell me which situation you would rather be in."<BR><BR>To combat the exodus caused by the lure of "Phat Lewtz" and perceived "Uberness" in the eyes of other players, many guilds are re-focusing their priorities on building a solid core and continually emphasizing the tradition and teamwork that are the hallmarks of a truly successful guild, though they might not be as compelling as insta-access to the Plane of Time.<BR><BR>Though fairly frequent guild changes are becoming a given in today's game, all is not lost for guilds who want loyal, passionate players, especially for tradition-rich guilds that have hit a minor bump in the road.  The strength of these guilds lies not in sheer numbers, nor in the amount of loot acquired, nor even in their progression or advancement through the game.  Rather their strength lies in the dedication and commitment of its loyal members - those committed to strive for excellence, even in the face of adversity and hardship.</BLOCKQUOTE></FONT><br>And for those people at whom this is targeted (and who might be a bit slow on the uptake), I have four words for you: Honor, Family, Loyalty, Honesty. Go look them up sometime. Then go look in the mirror. &nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Shaekee</a> on Thursday, June 19, 2003 at 01:50 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
